---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Local Focus — Eight34 Labs" description="Ridgewood first, then Bergen County, then New Jersey. In-person AI setup for local businesses, one town at a time.">
  <main>
    <section class="page-hero">
      <div class="hero-pill">
        <span class="status-dot"></span>
        <span>Local focus</span>
      </div>
      <h1>Ridgewood first. Then the county. <em>Then the state.</em></h1>
      <p>We&rsquo;re growing the way local trust grows — one town at a time, starting on East Ridgewood Avenue and working outward. If you&rsquo;re nearby, we can meet in person this week.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Rollout stages -->
    <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;">
      <div class="process-grid">
        <div class="process-step">
          <span class="step-badge">NOW · HOME BASE</span>
          <h3>Ridgewood, NJ</h3>
          <p>Where Eight34 Labs is based and where our first clients are. Downtown shops, restaurants, practices, and service businesses along Ridgewood Ave, Broad Street, and beyond.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="process-step">
          <span class="step-badge">NEXT · EXPANDING</span>
          <h3>Bergen County</h3>
          <p>The same in-person approach across the county — from our neighboring villages to Hackensack and the Route 4 / Route 17 corridors.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="process-step">
          <span class="step-badge">THEN · STATEWIDE</span>
          <h3>Across New Jersey</h3>
          <p>As the Bergen County practice grows, we&rsquo;ll bring the same playbook to main streets across the state — local first, at every step.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Towns -->
    <section class="section" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--ink-150);">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Communities in our Bergen County orbit</h2>
        <p>One town at a time, on purpose.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="towns">
        <li>Ridgewood</li>
        <li>Glen Rock</li>
        <li>Wyckoff</li>
        <li>Ho-Ho-Kus</li>
        <li>Midland Park</li>
        <li>Waldwick</li>
        <li>Fair Lawn</li>
        <li>Paramus</li>
        <li>Hackensack</li>
        <li>Teaneck</li>
        <li>Englewood</li>
        <li>Mahwah</li>
        <li>Ramsey</li>
        <li>Allendale</li>
        <li>Saddle River</li>
        <li>Westwood</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Who this is for -->
    <section class="section" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--ink-150);">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Who this is for</h2>
        <p>If customers know your name, this was built for you.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="services-grid">
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="num">RETAIL</span>
          <h3>Retail &amp; specialty shops</h3>
          <p>Customer questions, inventory, and follow-ups handled while you run the floor.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="num">FOOD</span>
          <h3>Restaurants &amp; cafés</h3>
          <p>Reservations, common questions, catering inquiries, and review follow-up.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="num">HEALTH &amp; FITNESS</span>
          <h3>Health, beauty &amp; fitness</h3>
          <p>Booking, reminders, intake forms, and re-booking regulars.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="num">SERVICES</span>
          <h3>Home &amp; professional services</h3>
          <p>Quote drafting, scheduling, job follow-ups, and invoicing without the evening paperwork.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Why local -->
    <section class="section" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--ink-150);">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Why local is the strategy</h2>
        <p>AI setup fails remotely. It works in person.</p>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size: 15px; color: var(--ink-500); max-width: 600px; margin-bottom: 40px;">
        The tools are the same everywhere. What makes them pay is fitting them to one specific business — its customers, its regulars, its way of doing things. That fit happens across a counter, not across a sales funnel.
      </p>
      <div class="services-grid">
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="num">REAL WORKFLOW</span>
          <h3>We see the real workflow</h3>
          <p>The way work actually moves through your shop on a busy Saturday is not in any onboarding form. Being nearby means the audit starts from reality, not from a questionnaire.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="num">NEIGHBORS</span>
          <h3>Your customers are our neighbors</h3>
          <p>A Ridgewood business lives on repeat customers and reputation. We configure escalation and tone accordingly — helpful and accurate, never a generic bot voice pasted onto your name.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="num">ACCOUNTABILITY</span>
          <h3>Accountability has an address</h3>
          <p>If something isn&rsquo;t working, you know where to find us. Local first is a commitment device: our next client is likely someone your client mentioned us to.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Rollout -->
    <section class="section" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--ink-150);">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>How the rollout works</h2>
        <p>One town at a time, on purpose</p>
      </div>
      <div class="process-grid">
        <div class="process-step">
          <span class="step-badge">RIDGEWOOD, NOW</span>
          <h3>Ridgewood, now</h3>
          <p>First clients, in-person audits, and setups we can support face to face. This is home base.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="process-step">
          <span class="step-badge">BERGEN COUNTY, NEXT</span>
          <h3>Bergen County, next</h3>
          <p>The same playbook for neighboring towns — Glen Rock, Wyckoff, Fair Lawn, Paramus, Hackensack, and the rest of the county — as word travels the way it does locally.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="process-step">
          <span class="step-badge">NEW JERSEY, THEN</span>
          <h3>New Jersey, then</h3>
          <p>Main streets across the state, only once the Bergen County practice is proven business by business. Growth follows results, not the other way around.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size: 15px; color: var(--ink-500); max-width: 600px; margin-top: 28px;">
        <strong style="color: var(--ink-900);">Outside the area?</strong> If you&rsquo;re beyond Bergen County and the fit is right, ask anyway — we&rsquo;ll tell you honestly whether we can serve you well yet.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Closing CTA -->
    <section class="section" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--ink-150); padding-bottom: 90px;">
      <div class="contact-cta-box">
        <h2>In our orbit — or about to be?</h2>
        <p>Tell us where you are and what your week looks like.</p>
        <div class="contact-cta-actions">
          <a class="btn-primary" href="/contact" style="padding: 12px 24px; font-size: 14.5px;">Contact Us →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
